sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Dashboard clients
    participant API as Simulation API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant P as Immediate publisher
    participant Q as Retry relay
    participant R as Redis pub/sub
    participant W as Subscriber and hub

    C->>API: Manager submits playback control
    rect rgb(230, 243, 252)
        Note over API,DB: One caller-owned database transaction
        API->>DB: SELECT simulation FOR UPDATE
        API->>API: Validate control against locked state
        API->>DB: Append control event and update projection
        API->>DB: Load schedule entries and control history
        API->>API: Build timeline and replay events
        API->>DB: Allocate sequence and insert outbox envelope
        API->>DB: COMMIT event, projection and outbox together
        Note over API,DB: A rollback persists neither the event nor its notification
    end

    API->>P: Publish committed outbox row
    P->>DB: Read unpublished row in separate transaction
    P->>R: PUBLISH validated simulation.changed envelope
    alt Redis accepts publication
        P->>DB: Mark published in a separate transaction
    else Publication fails
        Note over P,DB: Leave row unpublished for the relay
    end
    P-->>API: Attempt finished, delivery errors contained
    API-->>C: 200 authoritative position from committed control

    opt Unpublished rows are due
        Q->>DB: Claim batch with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        DB-->>Q: Locked due rows
        Q->>R: Retry PUBLISH
        alt Redis accepts retry
            Q->>DB: Mark published and commit relay transaction
        else Redis fails
            Q->>DB: Record failure and next_attempt_at, commit
            Note over Q,R: Stop batch, retry later with capped backoff
        end
    end

    Note over P,Q: Publish-before-mark races can produce duplicate messages
    Note over R,W: Redis acceptance is not a browser delivery acknowledgement
    opt A notification reaches a subscribed client
        R-->>W: Versioned change envelope
        W-->>C: WebSocket simulation.changed with playback anchor
        C->>API: Refetch current simulation through REST
        API->>DB: Load schedule entries and control history
        DB-->>API: Stored records
        API->>API: Build timeline and replay events at server time
        API-->>C: Position, playback flags and derived_at
    end
    Note over C,API: Refresh, reconnect and fallback polling use the same REST read
    Note over C,W: Notifications may arrive before or after the control response
